        "username": "MarioFanaticXV",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/{size}/2129_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-03T21:37:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>MarioFanaticXV wrote:</b><br><blockquote>However, there's a plethora of different super hero themed cartoons out there\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nYes and no.There's a fair number of Marvel/DC cartoons out there, but original property superhero cartoons is a question I'm not sure of.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>While I'll fully admit that the list is a lot looser with the concept of \"superhero\" than I'd like (Scooby-Doo and Star Wars are on the list?), if you go through the recent years manually searching for those that are still present, you'll find there's quite a number of them: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_superhero_television_series\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">List of superhero television series - Wikipedia</a></p>\n<p>And they have seperate pages for Marvel and DC.</p>",
