      {
        "id": 221832,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-03T22:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>While I'll fully admit that the list is a lot looser with the concept of \"superhero\" than I'd like (Scooby-Doo and Star Wars are on the list?), if you go through the recent years manually searching for those that are still present, you'll find there's quite a number of them:  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_superhero_television_series\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_superhero_television_series</a> And  they have seperate pages for Marvel and DC.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, that's why I asked here, since I first looked through that list and found it unhelpful since almost all of the series listed that I've heard of I wouldn't view as being superhero series. (Transformers and Mega Man? Really?)</p>\n<p>I think out of the ones currently running that I know anything of, there's maybe six? I'd consider superhero stories. And two of those are reboots.</p>\n<p>Interestingly there's not as many Marvel or DC series currently ongoing as I thought either.</p>",
